<title>SPAIN: Number of Spanish in work rose 354,100 in 1996.</title>
<headline>Number of Spanish in work rose 354,100 in 1996.</headline>
<dateline>MADRID 1997-08-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Spain put 354,100 more people to work in 1996 than in 1995, the Spanish statistical office INE said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>Unemployment fell by 43,500 people to give a rate of 22.21 percent of the active population, reflecting an economic recovery although the number of unemployed remains high at 3.54 million.</p>
<p>The number of working women continued to rise, reaching 36.98 percent, although it remains far behind the 45 percent prevailing in Europe in 1995.</p>
<p>The following table provides averages for the year in millions:</p>
<p>					   1996		1995</p>
<p>    Number working		  12.40		12.04</p>
<p>    Number unemployed		3.54		 3.58</p>
<p>Working rate (pct)</p>
<p>	    Both sexes		49.61		49.01</p>
<p>	    Men			 63.14		62.75</p>
<p>	    Women		     36.98		36.23</p>
<p>Unemployment rate (pct)</p>
<p>	    Both sexes		22.21		22.93</p>
<p>	    Men			 17.60		18.19</p>
<p>	    Women		     29.56		30.58</p>
<p>--Madrid newsroom +34 1 585 2167</p>
